resolution: |
  No L=4 (16x8) mean-removed vector codebook exists in this build.
  Not static-at-RVA: no contiguous signed-byte block of 12288 B
  (one half) or 24576 B (both halves) exists anywhere; the one
  signed-byte VQ region (vectors 0x67dcd224..0x67dd2c00, 23004 B; with
  the 36 B descriptor prefix the full region 0x67dcd200..0x67dd2c00 is
  23040 B = 2*(L0+L1+L2+L3)) is the L0..L3 intra+inter set and is
  bounded above by a float/resource blob.
  Not generated/derived at runtime: `analyze` (DllMain) writes 0 bytes
  that are later executed; no self-modifying/unpack step.
  Not compressed: the present codebook region is plain signed bytes
  (entropy ~4.1, mean ~0), not a compressed stream.
  Mechanism: 16x8 and 16x16 blocks are always subdivided to <=8x8
  before vector quantisation, so this level needs no codebook. The
  block-shape LUT (codebook-descriptor, values 1..4) and the absence
  of any *128 / *256 index scaling in .text corroborate this.
evidence_rvas: |
  codebook region   : 0x67dcd224..0x67dd2c00 (file 0x5d224..0x62c00)
  descriptor/LUT    : 0x67dcd200..0x67dcd224 (file 0x5d200..0x5d224)
  float/res blob end: 0x67dd2c00 onward (BM header at 0x67dd2c14)
